<title>GERMANY: YMOS says falls to H1 pre-tax loss.</title>
<headline>YMOS says falls to H1 pre-tax loss.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax loss			18.9     vs 10.3 profit</p>
<p>    Group sales				  494     vs 524</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German industrial group is YMOS AG.</p>
<p>YMOS said the reason for the drop in sales was the sale of its electrolyic oxidation parts business as well as weak sales of sanitary components due to slow construction conditions.</p>
<p>YMOS said the drop to a pre-tax loss was due solely to its domestic businesses, with foreign business operations reporting a profit of 5.2 million marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
